-------------------------------------------------------------

About CC multiple recipient email addresses.

CC is an acronym for carbon copy. In order to multiply sending
rates, messages composed by bulk mailers will often use a random
multiple-recipient CC addressing feature where one message is
sent to batches of addresses at a single time. This is also
believed to help email marketers thwart anti-spam filters.

UnsubscribeNow.org's OLX filtering system uses 676 online
spam-traps (26 A-Z x 26 a-z second tier letter variants) which
are harvested by email address scanners and propogated into their
mailing list. Single and multiple recipient email messages sent
to these trip lists are collected, their information is parsed
and an automatic responder is sent to attached addresses as the
Public Interest Announcement you have received today.

